-- title:
--   Gauss prolongations agree on L(f) for transcendental residue
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be a field and $A \subseteq L$ a valuation subring, with residue field $k = \mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$, and let $F$ be a field extension of $L$. Let $\bar F_1, \bar F_2$ be fields equipped with $k$-algebra structures, and let $R_1 : \mathrm{RegularProlongation}\,A\,F\,\bar F_1$ and $R_2 : \mathrm{RegularProlongation}\,A\,F\,\bar F_2$; thus each $R_i$ consists of a valuation subring $\mathcal O_i = R_i.\mathrm{integers}$ of $F$ together with a ring homomorphism $R_i.\mathrm{residue} : \mathcal O_i \to \bar F_i$ such that an element of $L$ lies in $A$ exactly when its image in $F$ lies in $\mathcal O_i$, the homomorphism is surjective with kernel the maximal ideal of $\mathcal O_i$, it is compatible with the residue map of $A$ via the $k$-algebra structure of $\bar F_i$, and every nonzero $f \in F$ admits $c \in L$ with $c \cdot f \in \mathcal O_i$ and $R_i.\mathrm{residue}(c \cdot f) \neq 0$. Assume $f \in F$ lies in both $\mathcal O_1$ and $\mathcal O_2$ and that its residues $R_1.\mathrm{residue}(f)$ and $R_2.\mathrm{residue}(f)$ are transcendental over $k$. Then for every $e \in F$ belonging to the intermediate field $L(f)$ generated by $f$ over $L$ inside $F$, one has $e \in \mathcal O_1$ if and only if $e \in \mathcal O_2$.
--
--   This is the uniqueness of the Gauss prolongation: a prolongation of $A$ to $L(f)$ under which the residue of $f$ is transcendental over the residue field of $A$ is determined on $L(f)$, so any two such prolongations induce the same valuation ring of $L(f)$. It is used in the construction of prolongations with prescribed residue data on a curve, in particular in the results producing a family of prolongations whose integer rings all extend a common Gauss ring and whose residue degrees sum correctly.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_RegularProlongation_mem_adjoin_iff_mem_integers_iff_of_transcendental_residue.lean

